# DTF tier manifest: quota-native-and-rpm-races
#   artifact-keeper#4422 (storage quotas enforced on every native publish,
#   PR #4543), #4421 (concurrent publishes of one RPM curated version, PR
#   #4497) and #4307 (concurrent RPM curated snapshot creates 500 with 40001,
#   PR #4389). All 1.11.0.
#   Profile-set: filesystem.
#
# THE BUGS
# * #4422: only the generic upload API, chunked uploads and npm publish ran
#   quota admission. Maven, Cargo, Conan, `docker push` (and ~25 other native
#   handlers) wrote their rows directly, so a repository grew past its
#   quota_bytes without a single refusal. The fix preflights before the bytes
#   are written and admits under the quota lock in the INSERT transaction: a
#   refusal is 507 {"code":"QUOTA_EXCEEDED"} (the registry envelope `DENIED`
#   for docker) and leaves no row. Manifests are charged 0 but a descriptor
#   with a negative or absurd size is now 400 MANIFEST_INVALID (it feeds the
#   usage ledger).
# * #4307: N parallel `POST /api/v1/curation/repos/{key}/versions` on one
#   RPM staging repository hit PostgreSQL serialization failures (40001)
#   past the retry budget and answered 500. Fixed: every create is 201 with
#   a distinct version number.
# * #4421: `mark_published` had no `published_at IS NULL` guard, so two
#   in-flight publishes of one version both rewrote the repodata (both 200).
#   Fixed: exactly one publishes, the others get 409 "Version N is already
#   being published by another request", and the signature verifies.
#
# The RPM staging repository is seeded the way the rpm-p3-curation tier does
# it: 30 approved curation_packages rows with structured primary metadata
# (inserted through DB_CONTAINER) and a GPG signing key with metadata signing
# on. The remote's upstream is never fetched.
#
# Gates: (CONTROL) a generic upload over the quota is 507 (enforced before
# 1.11.0 too) and a native Maven upload under the quota is 201; a curated
# version publishes, and its repomd.xml.asc verifies with gpg over
# repomd.xml with the served key (both images). (FIX) over-quota Maven,
# Conan, Cargo uploads answer 507 QUOTA_EXCEEDED and leave no artifacts row;
# an over-quota docker blob answers 507 DENIED and leaves no oci_blobs row;
# a manifest declaring a layer size of -1 is 400 MANIFEST_INVALID; four
# rounds of 16 parallel version creates are all 201 with 64 distinct
# numbers; four parallel publishes of one version give exactly one 200 and
# three 409s.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle fires 70 requests in bursts.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.10.0. Green: ak-backend:1.11.0 and main.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
